g in the gyre  is really important so uh different time  horizons will perform even for a little  increase in time horizon you can get  suddenly drastically good performance  and there's a histogram comparing the  energy spent or trajectories to what  how much energy or how much flow  velocity is in the background flow  but there's one more thing future work  so  with future work we're really interested  in so what we looked in this paper is  how one agent moves towards the  goal state essentially right but we can  also do one more thing where we can have  an  entire fleet of mobile sensors that are  all trying to move towards the goal  and this gives us a few ideas so we can  think about multi-agent coordination  where we're trying to get them all close  to each other or far away from each  other really quickly  or we can even understand how  uh the so when you have mpc acting  with the double jar it becomes this  entirely new dynamical system and we can  think of  oh what are the attracting regions in  this new dynamical system and how is  how do we quantify that and how do we  quantify control flow fields  and third we want to understand okay so  we  observed a lot of phenomena in  throughout this paper  and we want to understand okay  theoretically what is  producing all this why do mpc and fdle  have this connection  and so that's that's another direction  so thank you for listening to this talk  you can find the work on archive you can  you can play around with the code on  github
 

